      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "START CHEERING NZ (3) settled in the leading division and closed well to finish second last start over 1720m at Penrith. Has now been in the money three times from as many runs this prep. Sure to enjoy an economical run from this draw. Meets a comparable field and she can find winning ways. COOLABAH BILL (5) ran fifth last start at this track over 1609m, beaten 19 metres. Expected to run well. GATTUSO (10) is a two-year-old colt from the Rickie Alchin stable on debut. May need luck at some stage extracting from the inside of the second row. Showed some ability when a minor placegetter in a recent trial. Sure to prove tough to beat. NIGHT WITCH (9) broke in the run and 99th, beaten, first-up last time out over 1609m at this track. Should enjoy a nice smother from this draw and will be looking for a split at some stage. Live chance in a similar assignment.",
